    { "nodeId": "cpu", "message": "The active master drives address, control, and write data. It consumes read data, HREADY, and HRESP on the return path." },
    { "nodeId": "matrix", "message": "The interconnect carries the selected master's transfer. In a multi-master system it also multiplexes ownership." },
    { "nodeId": "decoder", "message": "This logical block combines address decode with the return-path mux. Implementations commonly place both functions inside the interconnect." },
    { "edgeId": "e-master-matrix", "message": "The two arrowheads do not mean every signal is bidirectional. Command and write data travel outward; read data, readiness, and response travel back." },
